              "end": 5,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the case concerns whether relief under the Convention Against Torture (CAT) affects the enforceability of a removal order."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that Congress defined the term \u201corder of removal\u201d as an order that finds an individual deportable or orders deportation, and that CAT relief does not disturb that order."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondent agrees that a grant of withholding or deferral leaves the final order of removal undisturbed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 65,
              "start": 65
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioner also points to regulation 8\u202fCFR\u202f1240.12(d), which requires an immigration judge to identify one or more countries to which removal is to occur."
      }
    ],
